From 56ab8db248f1e85021edce5e4649ef4923c2138c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:00:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] hc read: fast up projection on 320 / 640 blocks, bitwise
 the same (opt-in STRATA_GR_UP_SPLIT=2|4)

gr_up_fast_kernel (STRATA_GR_FAST) runs 16 columns (64 rows, 2 passes of 32 rows) a block at 128 registers:
160 blocks, 2 an SM, 16 warps an SM, and its token loop and lo staging have a run-time trip count.
STRATA_GR_UP_SPLIT=2 / 4 gives a block 8 / 4 columns (one pass of 32 / 16 rows, 256 / 128 threads, at most 64
registers so all 320 / 640 blocks are resident at once: 32 warps an SM), with an instantiation per token
count. Each row is still 8 lanes with the same chunks, combination and xor tree, and each column's 4 streams
sum in one block in the same order, so every output is the same bits. Not with a q8_1 image of `mixed`
(STRATA_QFUSE, whose counter takes two blocks a group): that read keeps the 16 columns.
The kernel's body is now a template that gr_up_fast_kernel instantiates at 16 columns: its SASS and all 89
fused_gr kernels' are identical to g3-1441-ll (cuobjdump; gr_down_v3_kernel<1, 5, true> differs between
identical compiles of the same source, ptxas, both before and after this change). gr_parity ctest arms:
up_split2 and up_split4_down_split2 (with the production switches), up_split2_generic (STRATA_NO_MULTI_GR=1);
fused_gr_bench's SPLIT lines cover the down x up arms.

